/*
Problem: Delete the Middle Node of a Linked List (LC 2095)
Topic: Linked List / Fast & Slow Pointers

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

Use two pointers:

• Slow moves one step.

• Fast moves two steps.

When fast reaches the end, slow will
be at the middle node.

Keep another pointer (prev) to the
node before slow so that the middle
node can be removed.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. If the list has only one node,
   return NULL.

2. Initialize:

   slow = head

   fast = head

   prev = head

3. Move:

   • slow by one step.

   • fast by two steps.

   • Update prev before moving slow.

4. When the loop ends, slow points to
   the middle node.

5. Remove it by:

   prev->next = slow->next

6. Return the head.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

1 → 3 → 4 → 7 → 1 → 2 → 6

Middle node:

7

After deletion:

1 → 3 → 4 → 1 → 2 → 6

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

1 → 2 → 3 → 4

Middle node:

3

After deletion:

1 → 2 → 4

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

The fast pointer moves twice as fast
as the slow pointer.

So when fast reaches the end of the
list, slow is exactly at the middle.

The prev pointer lets us bypass the
middle node.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n)

One traversal of the linked list.

Space : O(1)

Only a few pointers are used.

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Linked List / Fast & Slow Pointers
*/

class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* deleteMiddle(ListNode* head) {

        // Single node
        if (head->next == NULL)
            return NULL;

        ListNode* slow = head;
        ListNode* fast = head;
        ListNode* prev = head;

        // Find middle node
        while (fast != NULL &&
               fast->next != NULL) {

            prev = slow;
            slow = slow->next;
            fast = fast->next->next;
        }

        // Delete middle node
        prev->next = slow->next;
        slow->next = NULL;

        return head;
    }
};
